[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS001
TITLE: Pilot clearance content: aircraft identity, runway, sequence, clearance kind, and wind when the clearance needs it
STATEMENT: >>>
The pilot-facing interface shall carry aircraft identity, runway, sequence position when the aircraft is queued, clearance kind, and wind when the airport configuration supplies wind for a takeoff or landing. The readable phrase shall state those same facts in tower wording for runway assignment, sequence, hold short, line up and wait, takeoff, landing, and go-around. Acceptance is a landing clearance whose fields and phrase agree on the aircraft and the runway, and a takeoff clearance that includes the configured wind.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
FAA JO 7110.65 supplies the information content. The interface carries that content without pasting the order.
<<<
DAL: B
REQUIREMENT_LEVEL: Interface
VERIFICATION: Test
ASSUMPTIONS: Wind is optional in the TOML file. When it is absent, a takeoff phrase omits wind rather than inventing it.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS005
